.venv/
node_modules/
frontend/build/
frontend/.svelte-kit/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Everything under data/ is content, and content does not go in the repo. The
# repo holds the app; this machine holds what you have done with it.
#
# That means all of it: your trees, because you edit them in the UI and do not
# want a commit per season switch; the event log and checklist, because they
# are the record of your practice rather than part of the program; your notes
# and photographs, because they are private; and the index, because it is a
# cache that rebuilds from the log.
#
# The consequence is that the repo is NOT a backup. Every file below exists in
# one copy on this disk unless something else copies it — see SYNC.md.
#
# Written `data/*` and not `data/` on purpose: git does not descend into an
# excluded *directory*, so the negation below would never be reached.
data/*

# The same, for a data directory that has moved somewhere else and been left
# behind until its owner is sure. `data/*` does not cover a sibling name, and
# what gets left behind is by definition the whole of someone's history.
data.*/

# ...except the seed trees. These are the six researched curricula as shipped,
# not your live copies of them: read-only reference material that a fresh clone
# copies into data/domains/ once, and that `test_shipped_data.py` checks has
# not silently lost its estimates, gates or entry material.
!data/seed/

# The Trophic porting bundle: a copy of another repo's source, its schema, its
# UI notes and 2058 golden fixtures. Read once, ported from, and not part of
# this program — so it stays a local working copy rather than 17k lines of
# someone else's TypeScript in this history.
#
# The cost is real and worth knowing: `golden/verify_golden.py` lives inside
# it, so the port's oracle — and the parser adapter already wired into it —
# exist only on this disk. TROPHIC.md records where to fetch the bundle again
# and what to re-wire if it is ever re-copied.
#
# Leading slash, and it matters: an unanchored `trophic/` matches a directory
# of that name at *any* depth, which silently excluded the entire ported UI in
# frontend/src/lib/trophic/ and frontend/src/routes/trophic/.
/trophic/
